  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">2024 Syria Regional Appeal - Syria - emergency humanitaria assistance for basic needs</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Agency will continue to provide this assistance based on a targeted approach, prioritizing refugees assessed as most vulnerable with a higher cash transfer. In 2023, it is expected that around 155,500 Palestine refugees will be assessed as most vulnerable based on the four vulnerability categories used by UNRWA (female headed households, families with persons with disabilities, families headed by an older person and unaccompanied minors/orphans). A total of 420,000 Palestine refugees will receive cash assistance (vulnerable and most vulnerable). 60,500 households will be provided with winterization assistance (one-off NFIs).</narrative>
  </description>
